insert into public.knowledge_embeddings (content, source, section, metadata) values ($kb$Age-Based Navigation Timeline

BIRTH-3: Early Start/RC, IFSP within 45 days, transition planning at 2.5, IEP by 3rd birthday. Open CalABLE account.

AGES 3-5: IEP in place by 3rd birthday. Preschool placement. Apply SSI, IHSS. CalABLE.

AGES 5-11: Annual IEP. Triennial re-eval. Track service delivery (DRC log). IEE rights. Request additional assessments if new concerns. CalABLE.

AGES 11-14: Middle school transition IEP. ERMHS if needed. Prepare for ITP discussion. CalABLE.

AGES 14-17: ITP required at 16. Connect DOR. Post-secondary planning. Diploma vs Certificate decision. CalABLE.

AGES 18-22: SSI adult re-eval (apply immediately). Age of majority. Conservatorship/SDM decision. IEP until 22 or diploma. RC adult services.

AGES 22+: RC IPP. Supported living. Employment support (DOR/RC). IHSS. SSI CDR monitoring.

PLANNING: At each age, know what's coming next. Start transition planning 6-12 months early.$kb$, $kb$navigation$kb$, $kb$ent-age-timeline$kb$, $kb${"code":"ent-age-timeline","title":"Age-Based Navigation Timeline","category":"navigation","subcategory":"age-navigation-timeline","source_ref":"IDEA, DDS, SSA, CalABLE","origin":"entity-matrix-v9.4"}$kb$::jsonb);
insert into public.knowledge_embeddings (content, source, section, metadata) values ($kb$Equity Disparities in California Disability Services

Significant disparities exist across California's disability service systems.

REGIONAL CENTER: White children receive ~2x more spending than Latino children at 17 of 21 RCs. South Central LA RC: $1,991/child with ASD vs Orange County RC: $18,356 — 9x difference. DDS $66M equity initiative.

SCHOOLS: Hispanic/Latino 40% less likely identified with autism. Black children misdiagnosed with ID instead of autism. 10K+ teacher vacancies in rural/low-income. Black disabled students 3.63x more likely referred to law enforcement (DREDF data).

WHAT YOU CAN DO: Request all available services — don't accept only what's offered. Ask specifically about services other families receive. Request documents in your preferred language. File 4731 complaint if RC not providing equitable services.

SYSTEMIC SUPPORTS: DDS SAE grants fund disparity reduction. AB 1208 requires standardized quality measures. You have the right to appeal in your preferred language.$kb$, $kb$rights$kb$, $kb$ent-equity$kb$, $kb${"code":"ent-equity","title":"Equity Disparities in California Disability Services","category":"rights","subcategory":"equity-disparities","source_ref":"DDS SAE Data, Public Counsel 2022, AB 1208, DREDF","origin":"entity-matrix-v9.4"}$kb$::jsonb);
