Autism — Step 2.3: Private Diagnostic Evaluation (Optional but Valuable)

WHAT TO DO: PURSUE PRIVATE EVALUATION IF: (1) RC evaluation is delayed or incomplete. (2) You want a more detailed assessment (neuropsychological). (3) You want a second opinion. (4) You need a faster diagnosis to begin insurance-authorized ABA. HOW: Ask pediatrician for referral to developmental pediatrician or neuropsychologist. Insurance may cover — check your plan's behavioral health or neurodevelopmental evaluation benefits. Medi-Cal covers developmental evaluations. Wait times: 3-12 months for developmental pediatrician, 2-8 weeks for private neuropsychologist.

HOW TO ACT: STEP 1: Call your insurance company: 'Does my plan cover a neurodevelopmental or autism evaluation? What is my copay/coinsurance? Do I need a referral? Which providers are in-network?'
STEP 2: Ask pediatrician for referral letter to developmental pediatrician or neuropsychologist.
STEP 3: Call 3-5 providers to compare wait times. Ask to be on cancellation lists.
STEP 4: When you get the appointment, bring ALL RC evaluation reports plus your documentation.
STEP 5: After private eval, share results with RC to support eligibility determination AND with school district for IEP.

CONTACT: UNIVERSITY AUTISM CENTERS (CA):
• UCSF Autism Clinic: (415) 353-2101
• Stanford Autism Center: (650) 736-1235
• UC Davis MIND Institute: (916) 703-0280
• UCLA Autism Research: (310) 825-9011
• Children's Hospital LA: (323) 361-2178
• Rady Children's San Diego: (858) 576-1700
FINDING CA EVALUATORS:
• CA Psychological Association: cpapsych.org — find a psychologist
• Psychology Today directory: psychologytoday.com — filter by 'autism evaluation'
• Your insurance provider directory
INSURANCE COVERAGE:
• Call number on back of card — ask for 'neurodevelopmental assessment' or 'autism evaluation' benefits
• CA SB 946 requires commercial insurance to cover autism-related services

DOCUMENTS: PRIVATE EVALUATION REPORTS:
• Neuropsychological/developmental evaluation report
• Autism diagnostic report with DSM-5 criteria
• Recommendations for treatment

INSURANCE DOCUMENTS:
• Referral from pediatrician
• Insurance pre-authorization (if required)
• EOB (Explanation of Benefits) after evaluation
• Appeal materials if denied

TIMELINE: Private wait times: 3-12 months for developmental pediatrician. 2-8 weeks for private neuropsychologist. Insurance pre-auth: 5-15 business days. CANCEL LIST: Always ask to be on cancellation list — significantly reduces wait.

AVOID: DO NOT: (1) Assume private eval replaces RC eval — you need BOTH for different purposes (private = clinical diagnosis for insurance; RC = Lanterman eligibility for RC services). (2) Pay $3K-$6K out of pocket without checking insurance first. (3) Assume a long waitlist means no options — call multiple providers and ask to be put on cancellation lists. (4) Use an evaluator who is not autism-qualified (look for ADOS-2 certified).

RISKS: Insurance denies authorization. Long waitlists. Cost $2K-$6K out of pocket if uninsured. Private eval may use different criteria than RC. Results may not match RC findings. Medi-Cal covers but reimbursement rates low (fewer providers accept).

RESOURCES: INSURANCE NAVIGATION:
• Health Consumer Alliance: healthconsumer.org — free insurance help
• Medi-Cal Ombudsman: (888) 452-8609
• DMHC Help Center: (888) 466-2219 (HMO plans)
• CDI Consumer Hotline: (800) 927-4357 (PPO plans)
EVALUATION PREPARATION:
• Autism Speaks First Concern to Action: autismspeaks.org

PRIMARY AGENCY: Private Provider / Insurance
OTHER AGENCIES: Medi-Cal
