Autism — Step 3.2: Apply for Medi-Cal, SSI, IHSS, CalABLE (Full Benefits Package)

WHAT TO DO: APPLY FOR ALL FOUR BENEFITS SIMULTANEOUSLY: (1) MEDI-CAL: RC eligibility often opens HCBS-DD waiver pathway — only child's income counts (institutional deeming). Apply at coveredca.com or county social services office. (2) SSI: Apply at ssa.gov or local SSA office. For autism, the Function Report is CRITICAL — describe WORST day, not average day. High initial denial rate — plan to appeal. (3) IHSS: Apply at county IHSS office. Requires Medi-Cal. County worker does in-home assessment. Parent CAN be paid provider. Request protective supervision if applicable. (4) CalABLE: Open account at calable.ca.gov — no minimum age, $19K/year, doesn't affect SSI under $100K.

HOW TO ACT: MEDI-CAL: Apply online at coveredca.com or call (800) 300-1506. Contact your county social services office.
SSI: Apply at ssa.gov/benefits/disability or call (800) 772-1213. Bring: birth certificate, medical records, evaluation reports, school records.
IHSS: Apply at your county Social Services: your county IHSS office — cdss.ca.gov. Bring: Medi-Cal card, medical certification form (SOC 873), physician statement.
CalABLE: Open at calable.ca.gov (online, takes 15 minutes). Need: SSN, proof of disability.
STEP-BY-STEP: Start all 4 applications within the same week. Track each separately.

CONTACT: MEDI-CAL:
• Covered California: coveredca.com or (800) 300-1506
• Your county social services office
SSI:
• SSA: ssa.gov or (800) 772-1213
• Local SSA office (California): 150 Frank H Ogawa Plaza, California 94612
IHSS:
• your county IHSS: your county IHSS office — cdss.ca.gov
• IHSS Helpline: ihssunion.org for provider resources
CalABLE:
• calable.ca.gov (online enrollment)
HELP WITH APPLICATIONS:
• DRC: (800) 776-5746
• Health Consumer Alliance: healthconsumer.org

DOCUMENTS: MEDI-CAL: Application, income documentation, residency proof
SSI: Application, medical evidence, Function Report (SSA-3375), financial disclosure
IHSS: Application (SOC 295), Medical Certification (SOC 873), physician statement, Medi-Cal enrollment proof
CalABLE: Online application, SSN, disability documentation

KEEP COPIES OF EVERYTHING. Create a 'Benefits' folder with subfolders for each program.

TIMELINE: Medi-Cal: 45 days for determination. SSI: 3-6 months (plan for appeal). IHSS: 30-60 days from application to assessment. CalABLE: Immediate enrollment online. START ALL FOUR THIS WEEK.

AVOID: DO NOT: (1) Understate your child's challenges on SSI Function Report — describe the WORST day, not the best. (2) Skip IHSS because you don't know about it — many autism families qualify. (3) Forget CalABLE — open it immediately regardless of child's age. (4) Assume SSI denial is final — appeal rates are high and many win on appeal. (5) Let one application delay another — apply for all four simultaneously.

RISKS: ★ SSI denied initially (common — ~60% denial rate). Function Report is too positive. IHSS protective supervision denied. Medi-Cal redetermination causes gaps. CalABLE not opened early. Benefits interactions complex (SSI + IHSS + Medi-Cal). Parent doesn't know they can be paid IHSS provider.

RESOURCES: BENEFITS HELP:
• DRC SSI Guide: disabilityrightsca.org
• SSI denied? DRC Appeal Help: (800) 776-5746
• IHSS Advocacy: Personal Assistance Services Council
• CalABLE Info: calable.ca.gov/faqs
• Benefits calculator: db101.org (Disability Benefits 101)
PARENT TRAINING:
• Undivided benefits webinars: undivided.io
• Matrix Parent Network benefits training
• TASK benefits workshops: taskca.org

PRIMARY AGENCY: SSA (SSI)
DHCS (Medi-Cal)
County IHSS
CalABLE
OTHER AGENCIES: Regional Center
