insert into public.knowledge_embeddings (content, source, section, metadata) values ($kb$Autism Step 5.1: Insurance Authorization for ABA Therapy

Autism — Step 5.1: Insurance Authorization for ABA Therapy

WHAT TO DO: GET ABA THERAPY AUTHORIZED: (1) California law (SB 946) mandates health insurance coverage for behavioral health treatment (ABA) for autism — this includes Medi-Cal managed care plans. (2) Get physician referral/prescription for ABA from your pediatrician: 'My child has an autism diagnosis and I'm requesting a referral for ABA therapy.' (3) Call your insurance company: 'I need to start the prior authorization process for ABA therapy for my child who has an autism diagnosis.' (4) Choose an ABA provider — ask RC for their vendor list, also check insurance provider directory. Interview 2-3 providers before selecting. (5) ABA provider submits treatment plan to insurance. Typical request: 10-40 hours/week depending on severity. (6) If authorized, confirm: hours approved, duration, renewal process. (7) If denied, appeal immediately — CA parity law is strong.

HOW TO ACT: STEP 1: Get ABA referral from pediatrician (1 phone call — 'I need an ABA referral for my autistic child').
STEP 2: Call insurance (number on card): 'I need to begin prior authorization for ABA therapy. What is the process? What documentation is needed?'
STEP 3: Search for ABA providers: (a) Insurance provider directory, (b) RC vendor list, (c) bacb.com (BACB registry of certified analysts).
STEP 4: Interview 2-3 ABA providers. Ask: 'What is your supervision model? What is the BCBA-to-client ratio? Do you use naturalistic teaching? How do you involve parents? What does a typical session look like?'
STEP 5: Selected provider submits treatment plan to insurance. Insurance has 5-15 business days for prior authorization.
STEP 6: If APPROVED: confirm hours, start date, authorization period. If DENIED: appeal immediately — contact DRC or Health Consumer Alliance for free help.

CONTACT: INSURANCE COMPANY: Call number on back of insurance card. Ask for 'behavioral health prior authorization.'
MEDI-CAL MANAGED CARE: Each plan has its own ABA authorization process. Alameda Alliance: (510) 747-4500.
ABA PROVIDER SEARCH:
• BACB registry: bacb.com/find-a-certificant
• Insurance provider directory (online)
• RC vendor list (ask Service Coordinator)
IF DENIED:
• DMHC (HMO plans): (888) 466-2219 — Independent Medical Review
• CDI (PPO plans): (800) 927-4357
• Health Consumer Alliance: healthconsumer.org — free help
• DRC: (800) 776-5746

DOCUMENTS: INSURANCE DOCUMENTS:
• Physician referral for ABA
• Autism diagnosis report
• ABA treatment plan (from provider)
• Prior authorization request
• Authorization approval letter
• If denied: denial letter, appeal letter, medical necessity evidence

KEEP TRACKING:
• Authorization start/end dates
• Hours approved vs hours used
• Renewal deadlines
• Progress reports from provider

TIMELINE: Prior auth: 5-15 business days. If denied, internal appeal: 30 days. DMHC Independent Medical Review: 45 days. Urgent review: 72 hours. Authorization renewal: typically every 6-12 months.

AVOID: DO NOT: (1) Accept denial without appealing — CA law mandates ABA coverage for autism. (2) Wait for RC to provide ABA — insurance should be billed first (RC is payer of last resort). (3) Choose the first ABA provider without interviewing others. (4) Assume 'ABA' means one thing — quality varies enormously. Ask about their approach, qualifications, supervision ratios. (5) Let ABA hours be less than what the evaluation recommends without documented justification.

RISKS: ★ Authorization denied despite CA parity law. Insufficient hours approved. Provider not in-network. Medi-Cal managed care barriers. ABA waitlists 3-6 months. Quality varies enormously across providers. Authorization gaps between renewals.

RESOURCES: INSURANCE HELP:
• Health Consumer Alliance: healthconsumer.org — free insurance advocacy
• DMHC Help Center: (888) 466-2219
• CDI Consumer Hotline: (800) 927-4357
• DRC: (800) 776-5746
ABA QUALITY GUIDE:
• Autism Speaks ABA guide: autismspeaks.org
• BACB: bacb.com
• Association for Behavior Analysis International: abainternational.org

PRIMARY AGENCY: Private Insurance /
Medi-Cal
OTHER AGENCIES: Pediatrician
