insert into public.knowledge_embeddings (content, source, section, metadata) values ($kb$Autism Step 5.2: Begin and Coordinate All Therapy Services

Autism — Step 5.2: Begin and Coordinate All Therapy Services

WHAT TO DO: COORDINATE YOUR CHILD'S FULL SERVICE PACKAGE: (1) Your child may receive services from 3-4 DIFFERENT payers simultaneously: insurance-billed ABA, RC-vendored services (respite, parent training), school district IEP services (speech, OT, SDI), and potentially private pay therapies. (2) Create a MASTER SCHEDULE that accounts for all services without conflicts. (3) Ensure all providers communicate — school SLP, private ABA team, RC service coordinator should all know what others are doing. (4) You are the HUB of coordination — no one else will do this for you. (5) Track authorization dates, progress reports, and renewal deadlines for each payer.

HOW TO ACT: STEP 1: Create a spreadsheet or use a planner with: Service | Provider | Payer | Schedule | Auth dates | Renewal deadline | Progress report due dates.
STEP 2: Share your child's full service schedule with every provider. Ask each provider: 'Are you aware of my child's other services? How will you coordinate?'
STEP 3: Set calendar reminders for ALL renewal deadlines (at 60, 30, and 15 days before expiration).
STEP 4: Request progress reports from every provider quarterly. Compare progress across settings.
STEP 5: Hold a quarterly 'coordination call' or email update with all providers.

CONTACT: YOUR SERVICE COORDINATOR HUB:
• ABA Provider: BCBA supervisor (get direct number)
• RC Service Coordinator: direct number and email
• School IEP Case Manager: direct number and email
• Private therapists (if applicable): direct contacts
COORDINATION TOOLS:
• Google Calendar shared with providers
• Binder or digital folder organized by provider

DOCUMENTS: SERVICE TRACKING DOCUMENTS:
• Master service schedule (all providers/payers)
• Authorization letters (all payers)
• Progress reports (quarterly from each provider)
• Renewal deadline calendar
• Insurance EOBs (Explanations of Benefits)
• RC service authorization letters
• IEP service page

CREATE A 'SERVICE BINDER' with sections for: Insurance, RC, School, Private, Medical

TIMELINE: ABA waitlists: 2-6 months. Other services typically begin within 30 days of authorization. Insurance re-auth: every 3-12 months. IEP services: begin upon consent. RC services: begin upon IPP signing.

AVOID: DO NOT: (1) Let services overlap without coordination (e.g., school speech goals and private speech goals should align). (2) Miss authorization renewal deadlines — services stop if authorization expires. (3) Assume one provider knows what another is doing — they usually don't communicate unless you facilitate. (4) Over-schedule your child — leave time for play, family, and rest. (5) Forget to track which payer covers which service.

RISKS: Provider waitlists. Scheduling conflicts. Authorization gaps. Billing disputes. Providers don't communicate. Parent burnout from coordination burden. One change cascades across agencies.

RESOURCES: MANAGING MULTIPLE SERVICES:
• Undivided: undivided.io — service coordination tools
• Autism Speaks Resource Guide: autismspeaks.org/resource-guide
• Your ABA company's parent coordinator
SELF-CARE FOR PARENTS:
• FRCNCA support groups: frcnca.org
• Autism parent support: autismspeaks.org/family-services

PRIMARY AGENCY: Multiple providers
and payers
