insert into public.knowledge_embeddings (content, source, section, metadata) values ($kb$Autism Step 6.1: CalABLE, SNT & Age-18 Planning

Autism — Step 6.1: CalABLE, SNT & Age-18 Planning

WHAT TO DO: LONG-TERM FINANCIAL AND LEGAL PLANNING: (1) CalABLE: Open account at calable.ca.gov immediately — no minimum age. Save up to $19K/year. Balances under $100K don't affect SSI. Tax-advantaged growth. (2) Special Needs Trust (SNT): If your child will receive inheritances or large gifts, SNT protects SSI/Medi-Cal eligibility. Consult an SNT attorney ($2K-$5K to establish). (3) AT AGE 18: (a) SSI re-evaluation (child → adult criteria — PREPARE), (b) Conservatorship vs Supported Decision-Making decision, (c) Transition to adult RC services. (4) Start planning for age 18 by age 16. (5) Consider: Letter of Intent (non-legal document describing your child's daily life, preferences, needs — for future caregivers).

HOW TO ACT: STEP 1: CalABLE — go to calable.ca.gov TODAY. Click 'Open an Account.' Takes 15 minutes. Fund with even $25/month.
STEP 2: By age 14, consult an SNT attorney. Ask your RC Service Coordinator or DRC for referrals to disability-focused estate planning attorneys.
STEP 3: By age 16, begin age-18 planning: conservatorship vs SDM research. Read DRC's guide at disabilityrightsca.org.
STEP 4: By age 17, if pursuing conservatorship, retain attorney and file petition. If pursuing SDM, create SDM agreement with your child.
STEP 5: 6 months before 18th birthday: prepare for SSI adult redetermination. Update medical evidence, gather school records, prepare new Function Report.

CONTACT: INSURANCE AUTHORIZATION:
• CA SB 946: Commercial insurance MUST cover behavioral health treatment (ABA) for autism. No age cap, no visit limit, no dollar cap.
• DMHC (HMO complaints): (888) 466-2219 — file complaint if HMO denies ABA.
• CDI (PPO complaints): (800) 927-4357 — file complaint if PPO denies.
• Medi-Cal: Covers ABA through managed care plans and regional center.
FINDING ABA PROVIDERS:
• BACB registry: bacb.com — find certified behavior analysts by ZIP.
• Your insurance provider directory.
• Regional Center service coordinator — can help find vendored providers.
APPEAL DENIALS:
• Always appeal in writing within 30 days.
• DMHC/CDI Independent Medical Review: free, binding on insurer.
• DRC: (800) 776-5746 — insurance advocacy help.

DOCUMENTS: FINANCIAL/LEGAL DOCUMENTS:
• CalABLE account confirmation
• SNT trust document (if applicable)
• Letter of Intent (informal but critical)
• Conservatorship petition OR SDM agreement
• SSI adult redetermination materials
• Updated medical evidence for age-18 SSI
• Power of Attorney (if applicable)
• ABLE account contribution records

TIMELINE: CalABLE: Open NOW (no minimum age). SNT: Consult attorney by age 14. Conservatorship: Begin process 12-18 months before 18th birthday. SSI age-18 redetermination: Prepare 6 months before. Start ITP (transition plan) in IEP by age 14-16.

AVOID: DO NOT: (1) Skip CalABLE — every year of delay is lost tax-advantaged saving. (2) Put money in your child's name without SNT — it can disqualify them from SSI/Medi-Cal. (3) Wait until 17 to plan for age 18 — conservatorship takes 6-12 months to process. (4) Default to full conservatorship without considering SDM (Supported Decision-Making). (5) Forget the Letter of Intent — it's not legally binding but invaluable.

RISKS: ★ CalABLE not opened early. SNT not established — inheritance disqualifies benefits. Conservatorship pursued as default without considering SDM. SSI re-evaluation at 18 catches family off guard. Full conservatorship when limited would suffice. Costs of conservatorship ($3K-5K).

RESOURCES: FINANCIAL PLANNING:
• CalABLE webinars: calable.ca.gov
• SNT training: NAELA (naela.org) — find disability estate planning attorneys
• DRC publications: disabilityrightsca.org
• The Arc future planning: thearc.org/our-initiatives
• Disability Benefits 101: db101.org
• Undivided financial planning: undivided.io

PRIMARY AGENCY: CalABLE / SSA /
SNT Attorney /
Superior Court
OTHER AGENCIES: RC (adult transition)
