Autism — Step 6.2: Ongoing Authorization Renewals, Reviews & Lifetime Management

WHAT TO DO: MANAGE THE ONGOING SYSTEM PERMANENTLY: (1) Create a MASTER DEADLINE CALENDAR for: insurance re-auth (every 3-12 months), IHSS annual reassessment, SSI CDR (every 1-7 years), Medi-Cal annual redetermination, IEP annual review (every 12 months), IPP annual review (every 12 months), triennial re-evaluation (every 3 years). (2) Set reminders at 60, 30, and 15 days before each deadline. (3) Attend every annual IEP and IPP meeting prepared with updated concerns and goals. (4) Request progress reports quarterly from all providers. (5) Track any SERVICE CHANGES across agencies — one change often affects others. (6) Keep your 'Service Binder' updated continuously.

HOW TO ACT: STEP 1: Create a digital calendar (Google Calendar) with ALL deadlines. Share with spouse/co-parent.
STEP 2: Create a 'Renewal Prep' checklist for each agency.
STEP 3: 60 days before each deadline, begin gathering updated documentation.
STEP 4: 30 days before, submit renewal paperwork.
STEP 5: 15 days before expiration, follow up to confirm renewal is processing.
STEP 6: If any renewal is denied or delayed, contact DRC: (800) 776-5746.

CONTACT: ALL AGENCY CONTACTS (keep in one place):
• Insurance: [your plan's number]
• RC Service Coordinator: [name, phone, email]
• School IEP Case Manager: [name, phone, email]
• IHSS: Your county IHSS office — find at cdss.ca.gov/in-home-supportive-services
• SSA: (800) 772-1213
• Medi-Cal: (800) 300-1506
• ABA Provider: [company, BCBA name, phone]
• CalABLE: calable.ca.gov
IF PROBLEMS:
• DRC: (800) 776-5746
• OCRA: (800) 390-7032
• DMHC: (888) 466-2219

DOCUMENTS: MASTER DOCUMENT SYSTEM:
Create folders for:
1. INSURANCE: auth letters, EOBs, appeals
2. REGIONAL CENTER: IPP, POS authorizations, correspondence
3. SCHOOL: IEP, evaluations, progress reports, correspondence
4. SSI: applications, CDR responses, Function Reports
5. IHSS: assessments, hour authorizations
6. MEDI-CAL: enrollment, renewals
7. CalABLE/SNT: account records
8. MEDICAL: records, specialist reports
9. CORRESPONDENCE: all letters sent/received (dated)

TIMELINE: Insurance re-auth: every 3-12 months. IHSS: annual reassessment. SSI CDR: every 1-7 years. Medi-Cal: annual redetermination. IEP: annual review (every 12 months). IPP: annual review (every 12 months). Triennial re-evaluation: every 3 years. CalABLE: ongoing contributions.

AVOID: DO NOT: (1) Miss a renewal deadline — services stop immediately. (2) Assume renewals happen automatically — most require parent action. (3) Let one agency's change slip through without updating others (e.g., SSI income change affects Medi-Cal and IHSS). (4) Skip annual IEP/IPP meetings — these are your opportunity to update goals and services. (5) Throw away any documents — keep everything.

RISKS: ★ Missed renewal = service gap. Authorization expires before renewal processed. Parent overwhelmed by overlapping deadlines. One change cascades across agencies. Document loss. Provider turnover disrupts continuity. Benefits overpayment due to unreported changes.

