ADHD — Step 4.2: School District Evaluation — ADHD-Focused

WHAT TO DO: Assessment plan should include: psychoeducational testing (to identify co-occurring LD), behavioral/social-emotional assessment (BASC-3, Conners teacher rating), executive function evaluation (BRIEF-2), classroom observation during structured AND unstructured activities, parent/teacher interviews, review of existing ADHD diagnosis and medical records. REQUEST SPECIFICALLY: (1) Executive function assessment — critical for ADHD. (2) Behavioral observation during HIGH-DEMAND tasks. (3) Academic fluency testing (not just accuracy — ADHD impacts speed/efficiency). (4) Social-emotional assessment across settings.

HOW TO ACT: STEP 1: Assessment plan should include: psychoeducational testing (to identify co-occurring LD), behavioral/social-emotional assessment (BASC-3, Conners teacher rating), executive function evaluation (BRIEF-2), classroom observation during structured AND unstructured activities, parent/teacher interviews, review of existing ADHD diagnosis and medical records.
STEP 2: REQUEST SPECIFICALLY: (1) Executive function assessment — critical for ADHD.
STEP 3: (2) Behavioral observation during HIGH-DEMAND tasks.
STEP 4: (3) Academic fluency testing (not just accuracy — ADHD impacts speed/efficiency).
