ADHD — Step 4.4: 504 Plan Alternative (If IEP Denied or Preferred)

WHAT TO DO: Many children with ADHD receive 504 Plans rather than IEPs. 504 Plan may be appropriate when: ADHD impacts functioning but child doesn't need specialized instruction (just accommodations). Section 504 broader eligibility: disability that 'substantially limits one or more major life activities' (learning, concentrating, thinking, reading, communicating). 504 accommodations can include: extended time, preferential seating, movement breaks, reduced homework, organizational support, testing modifications, behavioral expectations adjustments. NOTE: 504 Plans do NOT include specialized instruction or related services — if child needs those, IEP is more appropriate.

HOW TO ACT: STEP 1: Many children with ADHD receive 504 Plans rather than IEPs.
STEP 2: 504 Plan may be appropriate when: ADHD impacts functioning but child doesn't need specialized instruction (just accommodations).
STEP 3: Section 504 broader eligibility: disability that 'substantially limits one or more major life activities' (learning, concentrating, thinking, reading, communicating).
STEP 4: 504 accommodations can include: extended time, preferential seating, movement breaks, reduced homework, organizational support, testing modifications, behavioral expectations adjustments.
STEP 5: NOTE: 504 Plans do NOT include specialized instruction or related services — if child needs those, IEP is more appropriate.

