insert into public.knowledge_embeddings (content, source, section, metadata) values ($kb$ADHD Step 4.5: IEP/504 Dispute Resolution

ADHD — Step 4.5: IEP/504 Dispute Resolution

WHAT TO DO: KNOW YOUR DISPUTE RESOLUTION OPTIONS FOR ADHD: (1) If school denies evaluation, denies eligibility, offers inadequate IEP/504, or fails to implement: you have legal rights. (2) CA dispute resolution in escalating order: (a) Informal — meet with principal/SpEd director, bring advocate; (b) ADR — facilitated IEP or mediation through CDE; (c) CDE Compliance Complaint — cde.ca.gov/sp/se/qa/cmplntproc.asp — within 1 year; (d) OAH Mediation — free, voluntary; (e) Due Process Hearing — formal proceeding, 2-year statute. (3) Common ADHD disputes: school denies OHI eligibility ('grades are too high' — ADHD impact is functional, not just academic), school provides 504 when IEP is warranted, accommodations not implemented consistently (substitute teachers don't follow 504), behavioral consequences instead of BIP (suspension for ADHD-related behavior violates IDEA), medication-related conflicts. (4) CRITICAL: ADHD-related suspensions — if your child is suspended 10+ days, IDEA requires a Manifestation Determination Review (MDR). If behavior is related to ADHD, discipline must be modified. (5) RESTRAINT AND SECLUSION protections: CA Ed Code §49005.

HOW TO ACT: STEP 1: Document the problem in writing: 'On [date], [specific accommodation] was not provided. This is the [Nth] occurrence.'
STEP 2: Request an IEP/504 meeting in writing: 'I'm requesting a meeting to address implementation concerns with my child's [IEP/504] plan.'
STEP 3: Bring an advocate to the meeting. Free advocacy: CASE (caseadvocacy.org), DRC ((800) 776-5746), your local CA PTI.
STEP 4: If informal resolution fails, escalate: File CDE compliance complaint at cde.ca.gov/sp/se/qa/cmplntproc.asp. CDE investigates and can order corrective action within 60 days.
STEP 5: For more complex disputes: request OAH mediation (free) through OAH at (916) 263-0880 or oah.ca.gov.
STEP 6: Last resort: Due Process hearing — consider retaining a special education attorney. DRC may provide free representation for significant violations.
STEP 7: If SUSPENSION is the issue: demand Manifestation Determination Review (MDR) if 10+ days total suspension. Is the behavior a manifestation of ADHD? If yes → school must modify discipline approach and conduct FBA/BIP.

CONTACT: ADVOCACY SUPPORT:
• CASE: caseadvocacy.org — free IEP/504 advocacy
• DRC: (800) 776-5746 — free legal services for disability rights violations
• DREDF: dredf.org — disability rights education and defense
• OCRA: (800) 390-7032 — if RC services involved
• CDE Complaint: cde.ca.gov/sp/se/qa/cmplntproc.asp
• OAH (Office of Administrative Hearings): (916) 263-0880 — mediation and due process
FOR CA FAMILIES:
• DRC SERR Manual: serr.disabilityrightsca.org
• Wrightslaw: wrightslaw.com/info/discipl.index.htm — discipline and ADHD
• Your local CA PTI: parentcenterhub.org
• COPAA (Council of Parent Attorneys and Advocates): copaa.org — find SpEd attorney
• Legal Aid: check your county's legal aid society

