TIMELINE: CDE complaint: 60 days. Due process: 45 days from filing.

AVOID: DO NOT: If district denies eligibility or provides inadequate supports: (1) Request another IEP/504 meeting

AVOID THESE COMMON PITFALLS: Parent doesn't know they can appeal. District claims 'good grades = no disability.' IEE denied or district offers inadequate IEE provider. Attorney fees prohibitive. Parent burned out from adversarial process.

RISKS: Parent doesn't know they can appeal. District claims 'good grades = no disability.' IEE denied or district offers inadequate IEE provider. Attorney fees prohibitive. Parent burned out from adversarial process.

