ADHD — Step 5.1: Insurance Authorization for ADHD Treatment

WHAT TO DO: ADHD treatment coverage: Medication — generally covered under prescription benefit (stimulants may require prior auth, step therapy). Behavioral therapy — covered under mental health parity (MHPAEA). Psychological testing/evaluation — coverage varies widely. Parent training — often NOT covered. Key: Mental Health Parity Act requires equivalent coverage for mental health conditions including ADHD. Medi-Cal covers ADHD evaluation, medication, and behavioral therapy. Private insurance: check formulary for preferred medications, prior auth requirements.

HOW TO ACT: STEP 1: ADHD treatment coverage: Medication — generally covered under prescription benefit (stimulants may require prior auth, step therapy).
STEP 2: Behavioral therapy — covered under mental health parity (MHPAEA).
STEP 3: Psychological testing/evaluation — coverage varies widely.
STEP 4: Parent training — often NOT covered.
STEP 5: Key: Mental Health Parity Act requires equivalent coverage for mental health conditions including ADHD.

CONTACT: CHADD PROFESSIONAL DIRECTORY: chadd.org — find ADHD specialists
CBT THERAPISTS: psychologytoday.com — filter by ADHD, CBT, children
PARENT TRAINING PROGRAMS: CHADD Parent-to-Parent (free), Triple P, PCIT (ages 2-7)
INSURANCE: Call number on card. ADHD medication + behavioral therapy covered under mental health parity (MHPAEA).
MEDI-CAL: Covers ADHD evaluation, medication, and behavioral therapy.
DMHC: (888) 466-2219 | CDI: (800) 927-4357

