• Insurance card and plan details
• Referral documentation (if required)
• Pre-authorization approvals
• EOBs (Explanation of Benefits) for each claim
• Denial letters (for appeal)
• Appeal letters with supporting documentation
• Prescription records
• Provider invoices

MEDICATION INSURANCE:
• Formulary tier information
• Prior authorization for non-formulary medications
• Step therapy documentation
• Cost comparison across pharmacies

TRACK:
• Annual deductible status
• Out-of-pocket spending for tax deduction (IRS medical expense >7.5% AGI)

TIMELINE: Prior auth: 5-15 business days. Formulary check: immediate.

AVOID: DO NOT: Parent training — often NOT covered

AVOID THESE COMMON PITFALLS: Preferred medication not on formulary — step therapy required (try cheaper option first). Prior auth delays for stimulant medications. Behavioral therapy sessions limited. Neuropsychological testing not covered or limited. Medication shortage compounds insurance issues. Out-of-network provider costs for specialists. Telehealth restrictions for controlled substance prescriptions.

RISKS: Preferred medication not on formulary — step therapy required (try cheaper option first). Prior auth delays for stimulant medications. Behavioral therapy sessions limited. Neuropsychological testing not covered or limited. Medication shortage compounds insurance issues. Out-of-network provider costs for specialists. Telehealth restrictions for controlled substance prescriptions.

