ADHD — Step 5.2: Access Behavioral & Organizational Therapy

WHAT TO DO: Evidence-based therapies for ADHD: (1) Behavioral Parent Training (ages 4-12): most supported by evidence. (2) CBT for ADHD (ages 12+): addresses organizational skills, time management, emotional regulation. (3) Organizational Skills Training (OST): evidence-based for academic organization. (4) Social Skills Groups: address peer relationship difficulties common in ADHD. (5) Executive Function Coaching: not therapy per se, but growing field for building skills. (6) Occupational Therapy: for sensory, motor, and organizational needs. CHADD offers free/low-cost parent education programs including online courses.

HOW TO ACT: STEP 1: Evidence-based therapies for ADHD: (1) Behavioral Parent Training (ages 4-12): most supported by evidence.
STEP 2: (2) CBT for ADHD (ages 12+): addresses organizational skills, time management, emotional regulation.
STEP 3: (3) Organizational Skills Training (OST): evidence-based for academic organization.
STEP 4: (4) Social Skills Groups: address peer relationship difficulties common in ADHD.
STEP 5: (5) Executive Function Coaching: not therapy per se, but growing field for building skills.

CONTACT: CHADD PROFESSIONAL DIRECTORY: chadd.org — find ADHD specialists
CBT THERAPISTS: psychologytoday.com — filter by ADHD, CBT, children
PARENT TRAINING PROGRAMS: CHADD Parent-to-Parent (free), Triple P, PCIT (ages 2-7)
INSURANCE: Call number on card. ADHD medication + behavioral therapy covered under mental health parity (MHPAEA).
MEDI-CAL: Covers ADHD evaluation, medication, and behavioral therapy.
DMHC: (888) 466-2219 | CDI: (800) 927-4357

DOCUMENTS: THERAPY DOCUMENTS:
• Therapist credentials and specialty
• Treatment plan (goals, frequency, methodology)
• Progress notes (request copies quarterly)
• Insurance billing documentation
• Session tracking (date, focus, homework)

ORGANIZATIONAL COACHING:
• Coach credentials (ADHD-certified)
• Coaching agreement
• Goal tracking sheets
• Executive function skill assessments (before/after)

SOCIAL SKILLS:
• Group curriculum description
• Progress reports
• Home generalization activities

TIMELINE: Therapy: weekly for 8-20 sessions typically. Parent training: 8-16 sessions. Ongoing as needed.

AVOID: DO NOT: (5) Executive Function Coaching: not therapy per se, but growing field for building skills

AVOID THESE COMMON PITFALLS: Long waitlists for ADHD-specialized therapists. Insurance limits sessions. Generic therapy not ADHD-specific. OT often denied for ADHD by insurance. Parent training programs not locally available. Executive function coaching not insurance-covered.

RISKS: Long waitlists for ADHD-specialized therapists. Insurance limits sessions. Generic therapy not ADHD-specific. OT often denied for ADHD by insurance. Parent training programs not locally available. Executive function coaching not insurance-covered.

