AVOID: DO NOT: Annual IEP/504 review should assess: (1) Are accommodations still appropriate for current ADHD presentation? (2) Are IEP goals addressing executive function development? (3) Has medication change affected school needs? (4) Are co-occurring conditions (anxiety, LD) adequately addressed? (5) Is organizational support scaling appropriately with increasing academic demands? (6) Does child need more/fewer supports based on current functioning? Key: academic demands INCREASE each year while ADHD supports should EVOLVE, not just continue unchanged

AVOID THESE COMMON PITFALLS: Same accommodations carried over without update. Executive function supports reduced as child ages (opposite needed — EF demands increase). Medication changes at home not communicated to school. Success with support

RISKS: Same accommodations carried over without update. Executive function supports reduced as child ages (opposite needed — EF demands increase). Medication changes at home not communicated to school. Success with supports used to justify removing them. Transition to middle school/high school with inadequate accommodation transfer.

