RISKS: ★ TRANSITION GAPS: Self-advocacy skills never taught — child always had adults advocating. College disability services require STUDENT to self-identify and request accommodations (different from K-12). IEP accommodations don't automatically transfer to college. Medication management transitions from parent to teen — gap in adherence. ADHD impulsivity + new freedom = higher risk period (substance use, risky driving, academic failure). Financial impulsivity without parental oversight.

