TIMELINE: Transition to adult care at 18-21. Ongoing.

AVOID: AVOID THESE COMMON PITFALLS: Gap in care during transition from pediatric to adult provider. Adult prescribers less experienced with ADHD. Stimulant medication stigma increases for adults. Workplace disclosure concerns. ADHD burnout. Relationship difficulties. Financial impulsivity consequences. Substance use risk (self-medication). Many adults only diagnosed after child's diagnosis — parental ADHD affects family dynamics.

RISKS: Gap in care during transition from pediatric to adult provider. Adult prescribers less experienced with ADHD. Stimulant medication stigma increases for adults. Workplace disclosure concerns. ADHD burnout. Relationship difficulties. Financial impulsivity consequences. Substance use risk (self-medication). Many adults only diagnosed after child's diagnosis — parental ADHD affects family dynamics.

