SLI — Step 1.2: Pediatrician Screening & Referral

WHAT TO DO: AAP recommends developmental screening at 9, 18, and 30 months (ASQ-3 or PEDS). Speech/language-specific concerns should trigger: (1) Hearing test — MUST rule out hearing loss as cause of speech/language delay. (2) Referral to SLP (Speech-Language Pathologist) for evaluation. (3) For children under 3: referral to Early Start (California Part C early intervention). (4) For children 3+: referral to school district for evaluation. Pediatrician should NOT wait — early intervention is evidence-based and more effective than 'watch and wait.'

HOW TO ACT: STEP 1: AAP recommends developmental screening at 9, 18, and 30 months (ASQ-3 or PEDS).
STEP 2: Speech/language-specific concerns should trigger: (1) Hearing test — MUST rule out hearing loss as cause of speech/language delay.
STEP 3: (2) Referral to SLP (Speech-Language Pathologist) for evaluation.
STEP 4: (3) For children under 3: referral to Early Start (California Part C early intervention).
STEP 5: (4) For children 3+: referral to school district for evaluation.

CONTACT: PEDIATRICIAN: AAP recommends developmental screening at 9, 18, 30 months (ASQ-3 or PEDS). Request hearing test + SLP referral.
AUDIOLOGIST: Hearing test is REQUIRED before speech evaluation. Ask pediatrician for referral or contact your county's Children's Audiology program.
REGIONAL CENTER (ages 0-3): dds.ca.gov/rc/listing — intake line at your local RC. Self-referral accepted.
CA NEWBORN HEARING SCREENING: If newborn screening was not done or showed concerns — contact CA DHCS Newborn Screening Program: (510) 412-1502.
ASHA PROFIND: asha.org/profind — find licensed SLPs by ZIP code, specialty, and language.
HELP ME GROW CA: Call 211 for developmental screening and referral in your county.

