• Developmental screening results (ASQ-3, PEDS, or M-CHAT if ASD concern)
• Hearing test results — REQUIRED before speech eval (audiogram or OAE)
• Referral letter to SLP or Early Start/school district
• Well-child visit notes documenting concerns

PARENT PROVIDES:
• Your observations journal with dated examples
• Video recordings
• Completed milestone checklists
• Any daycare/preschool teacher observations
• Family history of speech/language delays (relevant genetic factor)

TIMELINE: Hearing test: schedule ASAP. Early Start referral: services begin within 45 days. School district: 60 days from consent.

AVOID: DO NOT: Pediatrician should NOT wait — early intervention is evidence-based and more effective than 'watch and wait

