insert into public.knowledge_embeddings (content, source, section, metadata) values ($kb$SLI Step 5.2: Parent-Implemented Language Strategies (Home Program)

SLI — Step 5.2: Parent-Implemented Language Strategies (Home Program)

WHAT TO DO: Parents are the MOST IMPORTANT intervention agent — more time with child than any therapist. Evidence-based parent strategies: (1) Follow child's lead in play — comment on what they're interested in. (2) Expand and extend child's utterances ('Doggy!' → 'Big brown doggy!'). (3) Model correct production — don't correct, recast ('I seed a cat' → 'You SAW a cat!'). (4) Read together daily — pause, point, ask open questions. (5) Reduce questions, increase comments and descriptions. (6) Create communication opportunities (put desired items in sight but out of reach). (7) Narrate daily routines. Programs: Hanen 'It Takes Two to Talk' (language), Hanen 'More Than Words' (autism/limited communication), Mommy Speech Therapy (free videos).

HOW TO ACT: STEP 1: Parents are the MOST IMPORTANT intervention agent — more time with child than any therapist.
STEP 2: Evidence-based parent strategies: (1) Follow child's lead in play — comment on what they're interested in.
STEP 3: (2) Expand and extend child's utterances ('Doggy!' → 'Big brown doggy!').
STEP 4: (3) Model correct production — don't correct, recast ('I seed a cat' → 'You SAW a cat!').
STEP 5: (4) Read together daily — pause, point, ask open questions.

CONTACT: YOUR CHILD'S SLP: Ask for specific home practice activities at every session.
HANEN CENTRE: hanen.org — evidence-based parent programs:
• 'It Takes Two to Talk' — for language delays
• 'More Than Words' — for ASD-related communication
• 'Target Word' — for late talkers
ASHA PARENT RESOURCES: asha.org/public — activities organized by age.
READING ROCKETS: readingrockets.org — oral language activities that build literacy.
PUBLIC LIBRARY: Free storytime programs build language. CA State Library: library.ca.gov — find your local library.
FRCNCA: frcnca.org — parent support groups and information.

DOCUMENTS: FROM YOUR SLP:
• Written home practice activities (updated each session)
• Practice schedule recommendations
• Strategy cards or visual reminders for home
• Progress monitoring you can do at home

PARENT CREATES:
• Home practice log (date, activity, duration, child's response)
• Video recordings of practice sessions (share with SLP for feedback)
• Language-rich routine plans (mealtime, bath, play — built-in language opportunities)

HANEN PROGRAM MATERIALS (if enrolled):
• 'It Takes Two to Talk' guidebook
• Session handouts and strategy sheets
• Video coaching feedback

TIMELINE: Ongoing — daily embedded in routines.

AVOID: DO NOT: (3) Model correct production — don't correct, recast ('I seed a cat' → 'You SAW a cat!')

AVOID THESE COMMON PITFALLS: Parents correct child instead of modeling — increases anxiety and reduces communication attempts. Too much questioning ('What's this? What color?') becomes drill, not conversation. Parents compare to siblings or peers — increases stress. Home strategies not aligned with therapy goals. Parent burnout from 'always being the therapist.' Cultural differences in parent-child communication styles not respected.

RISKS: Parents correct child instead of modeling — increases anxiety and reduces communication attempts. Too much questioning ('What's this? What color?') becomes drill, not conversation. Parents compare to siblings or peers — increases stress. Home strategies not aligned with therapy goals. Parent burnout from 'always being the therapist.' Cultural differences in parent-child communication styles not respected.

