SLD — Step 4.1: Section 504 Plan (If IEP Denied or Preferred)

WHAT TO DO: 504 PLAN AS ALTERNATIVE OR SUPPLEMENT: (1) If IEP denied because child doesn't need 'specially designed instruction' but HAS a disability affecting a major life activity (learning, reading, concentrating) — 504 Plan provides ACCOMMODATIONS. (2) 504 has BROADER eligibility than IEP — any disability that 'substantially limits' a major life activity. (3) 504 accommodations can include everything on the IEP accommodation list EXCEPT specially designed instruction and related services. (4) Many students with LD get 504 Plans, especially: milder LD, students whose grades are adequate with accommodations, students transitioning off IEP. (5) 504 is ALSO the bridge to college/SAT/ACT accommodations — accommodation history is critical for testing accommodation approval.

HOW TO ACT: STEP 1: If IEP denied, immediately request 504 evaluation: 'Since my child was not found eligible for an IEP, I request a Section 504 evaluation. My child has [LD type] which substantially limits learning/reading/concentrating.'
STEP 2: Provide documentation: evaluation reports, private eval, medical documentation, teacher input.
STEP 3: At 504 meeting, present comprehensive accommodation list (not just extra time). Include AT.
STEP 4: Get the 504 plan IN WRITING with specific accommodations, review schedule, and contact person.
STEP 5: Monitor implementation quarterly — email teachers: 'Is [child] receiving all 504 accommodations? Are there any challenges?'
STEP 6: Keep detailed records of 504 history — you WILL need this for SAT/ACT College Board accommodation requests.

CONTACT: SCHOOL 504 COORDINATOR: Every school has one — often the principal or counselor. Ask the front office.
CA STATEWIDE: Contact your school's 504 coordinator (typically principal or counselor).
IF 504 NOT OFFERED:
• DRC: (800) 776-5746
• OCR (Office for Civil Rights): ed.gov/ocr — file complaint if 504 rights violated
• OCR complaint hotline: (800) 421-3481
FOR SAT/ACT ACCOMMODATIONS:
• College Board SSD: collegeboard.org/students-with-disabilities
• ACT accommodations: act.org/the-act/accommodations

DOCUMENTS: 504 DOCUMENTS:
• 504 evaluation documentation
• 504 Plan (written, with specific accommodations)
• Annual 504 review documentation
• Teacher acknowledgment of accommodations
• Implementation tracking records

FOR FUTURE USE:
• Complete 504 accommodation history (needed for SAT/ACT/college)
• All evaluation reports supporting LD diagnosis
• Documentation of accommodation use and effectiveness
• College Board/ACT accommodation applications

TIMELINE: No specific federal timeline for 504 — push for completion within 30 days. 504 reviewed annually. OCR complaint: file within 180 days of violation. SAT/ACT accommodation requests: submit 6+ months before test date.

AVOID: DO NOT: (1) Accept 504 if your child needs SPECIALIZED INSTRUCTION — 504 only provides accommodations, not teaching methodology changes. (2) Forget that 504 has no federal timeline requirements — push for prompt development. (3) Accept a generic 504 with only 'extra time.' (4) Let 504 substitute for IEP when IEP is warranted. (5) Forget to document the 504 accommodation history — you'll need it for SAT/ACT/college accommodations. (6) Let the school ignore the 504 — there's no progress monitoring like IEP, so YOU must track implementation.

RISKS: ★ 504 RISKS: (1) Not offered when IEP denied — parent doesn't know to ask. (2) Generic plan (extra time only). (3) No enforcement mechanism — teachers may not implement. (4) No progress monitoring. (5) Annual review skipped. (6) SAT/ACT accommodation denied because accommodation history not documented. (7) College disability services harder to access without strong 504 history.

RESOURCES: 504 PLAN RESOURCES:
• Understood 504 guide: understood.org/en/articles/the-difference-between-ieps-and-504-plans
• Wrightslaw 504: wrightslaw.com/info/sec504.index.htm
• DRC 504 rights: disabilityrightsca.org
• OCR: ed.gov/ocr — complaint process
• College Board SSD: collegeboard.org/students-with-disabilities
• LDA 504 guide: ldaamerica.org

PRIMARY AGENCY: Local School District
(504 Coordinator)
OTHER AGENCIES: Parent
Teacher
