insert into public.knowledge_embeddings (content, source, section, metadata) values ($kb$ID Step 1.2: Referral to Regional Center (Self-Referral, Any Age)

ID — Step 1.2: Referral to Regional Center (Self-Referral, Any Age)

WHAT TO DO: California Regional Centers are the PRIMARY service system for intellectual disability. ID is one of the 5 qualifying Lanterman Act conditions (ID, cerebral palsy, epilepsy, autism, 5th category). Self-referral accepted at any age — no doctor referral required. For children under 3: Regional Center provides Early Start (Part C) services. For children 3+: Regional Center provides ongoing service coordination AND school district provides IEP. KEY: ID qualifies for BOTH Regional Center services AND school district special education — DUAL SYSTEM. This is different from SLD/ADHD which are school-district only.

HOW TO ACT: STEP 1: California Regional Centers are the PRIMARY service system for intellectual disability.
STEP 2: ID is one of the 5 qualifying Lanterman Act conditions (ID, cerebral palsy, epilepsy, autism, 5th category).
STEP 3: Self-referral accepted at any age — no doctor referral required.
STEP 4: For children under 3: Regional Center provides Early Start (Part C) services.
STEP 5: For children 3+: Regional Center provides ongoing service coordination AND school district provides IEP.

CONTACT: YOUR LOCAL REGIONAL CENTER: dds.ca.gov/rc/listing — call intake line. Say: 'I'd like to refer my child for a developmental evaluation. I have concerns about [cognitive development/adaptive skills/learning].'
CA DDS (Dept of Developmental Services): dds.ca.gov — oversees all 21 Regional Centers.
DRC (Disability Rights California): (800) 776-5746 — if RC delays intake beyond 15 working days.
OCRA (Office of Clients' Rights Advocacy): (800) 390-7032 — free advocacy for RC intake issues.
FRCNCA: frcnca.org — peer support during the referral process.
UNDIVIDED: undivided.io — free family navigator service to help with RC referral.

DOCUMENTS: TO BRING TO RC INTAKE:
• Child's birth certificate (copy)
• Proof of CA residency (utility bill, lease)
• Medi-Cal card or insurance card
• Medical records (if available, NOT required)
• Your observations journal and videos
• Any prior evaluations or medical reports

RC WILL PROVIDE:
• Referral acknowledgment letter
• Rights booklet (Lanterman Act rights — in your language)
• Consent for evaluation forms
• Service coordinator assignment
• Intake assessment form

PARENT TRACKS:
• Date of referral (starts 15-working-day intake clock)
• Service coordinator name and direct contact
• 120-day evaluation completion deadline

TIMELINE: RC must complete intake within 15 working days of referral.

AVOID: AVOID THESE COMMON PITFALLS: Family doesn't know about Regional Center. Family referred only to school district — misses RC services. Language barriers prevent self-referral. RC intake delayed. Family told child is 'too young' or 'not delayed enough' for referral.

RISKS: Family doesn't know about Regional Center. Family referred only to school district — misses RC services. Language barriers prevent self-referral. RC intake delayed. Family told child is 'too young' or 'not delayed enough' for referral.

