insert into public.knowledge_embeddings (content, source, section, metadata) values ($kb$ID Step 2.3: Process Diagnosis — Emotional Support & Next Steps

ID — Step 2.3: Process Diagnosis — Emotional Support & Next Steps

WHAT TO DO: ID diagnosis often triggers profound grief, fear, and uncertainty for families. Key support: (1) Connect with peer families — Family Resource Centers (FRCNCA), UC Davis MIND Institute Family Navigator, Parents Helping Parents (PHP). (2) Understand that diagnosis opens doors to services and supports. (3) Begin learning about dual system (RC + school). (4) Join parent support groups (online and in-person). (5) Learn about person-first language and strengths-based approach. (6) Connect with The Arc (national) and local Arc chapters. Programs: UC Davis MIND Institute — peer support, monthly virtual groups, parent coaching, Padres Para Padres (Spanish). FRCNCA — statewide network of family resource centers.

HOW TO ACT: STEP 1: ID diagnosis often triggers profound grief, fear, and uncertainty for families.
STEP 2: Key support: (1) Connect with peer families — Family Resource Centers (FRCNCA), UC Davis MIND Institute Family Navigator, Parents Helping Parents (PHP).
STEP 3: (2) Understand that diagnosis opens doors to services and supports.
STEP 4: (3) Begin learning about dual system (RC + school).
STEP 5: (4) Join parent support groups (online and in-person).

CONTACT: UC DAVIS MIND INSTITUTE FAMILY NAVIGATOR: health.ucdavis.edu/mindinstitute — peer support after diagnosis, monthly virtual groups, Padres Para Padres (Spanish-language), caregiver communities.
FRCNCA: frcnca.org — parent-to-parent support, local Family Resource Centers throughout CA.
