insert into public.knowledge_embeddings (content, source, section, metadata) values ($kb$ID Step 4.3: IEP Dispute Resolution — ID-Specific Issues

ID — Step 4.3: IEP Dispute Resolution — ID-Specific Issues

WHAT TO DO: Common ID-specific disputes: (1) Overly restrictive placement. (2) Failure to provide inclusion supports. (3) Inadequate behavioral support. (4) ESY denied. (5) Transition services inadequate. (6) Larry P. violations. Remedies: IEP meeting request → CDE state complaint (60 days) → mediation → due process (45 days). Disability Rights California (DRC) provides free advocacy for ID families. The Arc provides advocacy resources and local chapter support. Key: ID families more frequently face placement disputes than families of children with ADHD or SLD.

HOW TO ACT: STEP 1: Common ID-specific disputes: (1) Overly restrictive placement.
STEP 2: (2) Failure to provide inclusion supports.
STEP 3: (3) Inadequate behavioral support.
STEP 4: (5) Transition services inadequate.
STEP 5: Remedies: IEP meeting request → CDE state complaint (60 days) → mediation → due process (45 days).

CONTACT: DRC (Disability Rights California): (800) 776-5746 — free legal advocacy for SpEd disputes.
CDE COMPLAINT: cde.ca.gov/sp/se/qa/cmplntproc.asp — file compliance complaint (free, 60-day resolution).
OAH (Office of Administrative Hearings): (916) 263-0880 — mediation (free, voluntary) and due process hearing.
FAMILY EMPOWERMENT CENTERS: cde.ca.gov/sp/se/qa/fecprgm.asp — free advocacy support.
DREDF: dredf.org — Disability Rights Education & Defense Fund, Berkeley-based.
OCRA: (800) 390-7032 — if dispute involves both RC and school.
2-YEAR STATUTE OF LIMITATIONS: File within 2 years of the action you're disputing.

DOCUMENTS: DISPUTE DOCUMENTS:
• Written record of disagreement with district decision
• Prior Written Notice from district (they must provide when refusing parent request)
• CDE Compliance Complaint form: cde.ca.gov/sp/se/qa/cmplntproc.asp
• Mediation request through OAH: oah.ca.gov
• Due process complaint (if needed): oah.ca.gov

COMMON ID-SPECIFIC DISPUTES:
• Segregated placement vs inclusion — document LRE research
• Larry P. violation — document prohibited IQ testing
• ESY denial — document regression evidence
• Insufficient related services — document needs

KEEP:
• All correspondence with district
• Timeline of dispute
• 2-YEAR statute of limitations — file within 2 years

TIMELINE: CDE complaint: 60 days. Due process: 45 days.

AVOID: AVOID THESE COMMON PITFALLS: Family doesn't know about DRC free services. Attorney fees prohibitive. District 'stays put' in segregated placement during dispute. Family intimidated by process. Non-English-speaking families face additional barriers. Larry P. violations not reported.

RISKS: Family doesn't know about DRC free services. Attorney fees prohibitive. District 'stays put' in segregated placement during dispute. Family intimidated by process. Non-English-speaking families face additional barriers. Larry P. violations not reported.

