insert into public.knowledge_embeddings (content, source, section, metadata) values ($kb$ID Step 7.1: Begin Transition Planning — ITP Required

ID — Step 7.1: Begin Transition Planning — ITP Required

WHAT TO DO: Transition planning for ID is MORE COMPLEX than any other disability category because it involves both school district AND Regional Center adult services. By age 14-16: ITP (Individual Transition Plan) within IEP. Key areas: (1) Post-secondary education/training (community college disability services, adult education, certificate programs). (2) Employment (supported employment, customized employment, competitive integrated employment — CIE). (3) Independent living (supported living, independent living, residential care). (4) Community participation. (5) Self-advocacy and self-determination. Connect to DOR (Dept of Rehabilitation) by age 16. Connect to RC adult services planning by age 16-17.

HOW TO ACT: STEP 1: Transition planning for ID is MORE COMPLEX than any other disability category because it involves both school district AND Regional Center adult services.
STEP 2: By age 14-16: ITP (Individual Transition Plan) within IEP.
STEP 3: Key areas: (1) Post-secondary education/training (community college disability services, adult education, certificate programs).
STEP 4: (2) Employment (supported employment, customized employment, competitive integrated employment — CIE).
STEP 5: (3) Independent living (supported living, independent living, residential care).

CONTACT: SCHOOL TRANSITION COORDINATOR: Part of IEP team starting at age 14-16.
CA DOR (Dept of Rehabilitation): dor.ca.gov — vocational rehabilitation. Refer through IEP by age 16. DOR works with school to develop employment goals.
REGIONAL CENTER: Transition-age services (16-22). Day programs, supported employment, independent living.
WORKABILITY I: cde.ca.gov/sp/se/sr/wrkabltyi.asp — CA school-based employment program for SpEd students.
PROJECT SEARCH: projectsearch.us — internship-to-employment program for IDD.
FAMILY EMPOWERMENT CENTERS: cde.ca.gov/sp/se/qa/fecprgm.asp — transition planning advocacy.
THE ARC: thearc.org — Achieve with Us employment program.

DOCUMENTS: TRANSITION DOCUMENTS:
• ITP (Individual Transition Plan) in IEP — required by age 16 (start at 14)
• Transition assessments: vocational, functional, independent living
• Post-secondary goals: education, employment, independent living
• DOR referral documentation (by age 16)
• WorkAbility I program enrollment (if available at school)
• Project SEARCH application (if available in your area)

COORDINATE ACROSS SYSTEMS:
• School IEP with ITP
• RC IPP with transition goals
• DOR Individualized Plan for Employment (IPE)
• SSA adult redetermination prep (starts at 18)
• ★ THIS IS THE MOST COMPLEX TRANSITION — 4 systems simultaneously

TIMELINE: ITP required by age 16 (begin earlier). DOR connection by 16. RC adult planning by 17.

AVOID: AVOID THESE COMMON PITFALLS: TRANSITION CLIFF: School services end at 22 or diploma — adult services don't seamlessly replace them. RC adult services have waitlists. DOR vocational services limited. Supported employment underutilized (sheltered workshops still common despite evidence for CIE). Conservatorship pursued when less restrictive alternatives (SDM) would suffice. SSI transition from child to adult criteria at 18 — many lose benefits. Housing crisis for adults with ID.

RISKS: ★ TRANSITION CLIFF: School services end at 22 or diploma — adult services don't seamlessly replace them. RC adult services have waitlists. DOR vocational services limited. Supported employment underutilized (sheltered workshops still common despite evidence for CIE). Conservatorship pursued when less restrictive alternatives (SDM) would suffice. SSI transition from child to adult criteria at 18 — many lose benefits. Housing crisis for adults with ID.

