insert into public.knowledge_embeddings (content, source, section, metadata) values ($kb$ID Step 8.1: Ongoing Benefits Management & Monitoring

ID — Step 8.1: Ongoing Benefits Management & Monitoring

WHAT TO DO: Lifelong benefits coordination: SSI CDR (Continuing Disability Review) every 1-7 years. IHSS annual reassessment. Medi-Cal annual renewal. CalABLE contributions and spending tracking. SNT (Special Needs Trust) if assets exceed SSI/Medi-Cal limits. SSI and IHSS amounts adjust with living situation changes. Report changes to SSA within 10 days (overpayment risk). Benefits coordination for working adults with ID — PASS (Plan to Achieve Self-Support), IRWE (Impairment-Related Work Expenses), 1619(b) for Medi-Cal retention.

HOW TO ACT: STEP 1: Lifelong benefits coordination: SSI CDR (Continuing Disability Review) every 1-7 years.
STEP 2: IHSS annual reassessment.
STEP 3: Medi-Cal annual renewal.
STEP 4: CalABLE contributions and spending tracking.
STEP 5: SNT (Special Needs Trust) if assets exceed SSI/Medi-Cal limits.

CONTACT: SSA: ssa.gov — (800) 772-1213 — SSI CDR (Continuing Disability Review) every 1-7 years. Report changes.
IHSS: Your county IHSS office — annual reassessment. CA DSS: cdss.ca.gov/in-home-supportive-services
MEDI-CAL: Annual renewal through your county human services agency.
CALABLE: calable.ca.gov — monitor contribution limits ($19K/year, $100K SSI-safe threshold).
DRC: (800) 776-5746 — benefits counseling, appeal denied benefits.
HEALTH CONSUMER ALLIANCE: healthconsumer.org — help with Medi-Cal issues.
YOUR RC SERVICE COORDINATOR: Annual IPP review, service authorization renewals.

DOCUMENTS: BENEFITS TRACKING DOCUMENTS:
• SSI CDR (Continuing Disability Review) — every 1-7 years depending on category
• IHSS annual reassessment
• Medi-Cal annual renewal
• CalABLE contribution and balance tracking ($19K/year limit, $100K SSI-safe)
• SNT annual accounting (if applicable)
• RC IPP annual review
• Insurance authorization renewals

★ MASTER DEADLINE CALENDAR:
• SSI CDR date
• IHSS reassessment date
• Medi-Cal renewal date
• CalABLE contribution tracker
• IPP annual review date
• IEP annual review date (if still in school)
• Conservatorship annual accounting date

TIMELINE: SSI CDR: every 1-7 years. IHSS: annual. Medi-Cal: annual. Ongoing monitoring.

AVOID: AVOID THESE COMMON PITFALLS: Benefits overpayment due to unreported changes. CDR results in loss of benefits (requires appeal). IHSS hours reduced at reassessment. CalABLE/SNT coordination errors. Working adults lose benefits unexpectedly. Complex benefits rules overwhelm families.

RISKS: Benefits overpayment due to unreported changes. CDR results in loss of benefits (requires appeal). IHSS hours reduced at reassessment. CalABLE/SNT coordination errors. Working adults lose benefits unexpectedly. Complex benefits rules overwhelm families.

RESOURCES: THE ARC: thearc.org — advocacy tools, policy updates, community inclusion, local chapters
FRCNCA: frcnca.org — peer support, advocacy training, language-accessible
UC DAVIS MIND INSTITUTE: health.ucdavis.edu/mindinstitute — peer groups, parent coaching, Spanish-language support
PARENTS HELPING PARENTS: php.com — consultations, webinars, support groups
DRC PUBLICATIONS: disabilityrightsca.org — RC rights, conservatorship, SSI guides (free, multilingual)
UCP: ucp.org — My Child Without Limits community
SELF-DETERMINATION PROGRAM: CA self-determination for RC clients
CA PTI NETWORK: parentcenterhub.org
BOOKS: 'The Complete Guide to Special Education' (Wilmshurst/Brue)

PRIMARY AGENCY: SSA / IHSS / Medi-Cal / CalABLE
CalABLE DETAILS: calable.ca.gov — tax-advantaged savings account (up to $100K without affecting SSI/Medi-Cal). Eligible if disability onset before age 26. Funds usable for housing, education, health, employment, assistive technology, transportation, and more.
OTHER AGENCIES: Regional Center
Financial planner
SNT trustee$kb$, $kb$journey_id$kb$, $kb$jrn-id-s81$kb$, $kb${"code":"jrn-id-s81","title":"ID Step 8.1: Ongoing Benefits Management & Monitoring","category":"journey-id","subcategory":"step-81","source_ref":"Entity Matrix v9.4","origin":"entity-matrix-v9.4"}$kb$::jsonb);
insert into public.knowledge_embeddings (content, source, section, metadata) values ($kb$ID Step 8.2: Long-Term Advocacy & Community Engagement

ID — Step 8.2: Long-Term Advocacy & Community Engagement

WHAT TO DO: Lifelong advocacy needs for individuals with ID: (1) The Arc: largest national IDD advocacy organization — local chapters, policy advocacy, community inclusion programs, Achieve with Us employment network. (2) Self-advocacy: People First movement, self-advocacy groups. (3) Voting rights: most individuals with ID CAN vote (conservatorship may affect this — know your rights). (4) Community inclusion: friendships, recreation, faith community, civic participation. (5) Health advocacy: preventive care, mental health access, healthy aging (life expectancy for ID has increased dramatically but healthcare disparities persist). (6) Policy advocacy: Lanterman Act protection, DDS budget, HCBS settings rule, Employment First policy.

HOW TO ACT: STEP 1: Lifelong advocacy needs for individuals with ID: (1) The Arc: largest national IDD advocacy organization — local chapters, policy advocacy, community inclusion programs, Achieve with Us employment network.
STEP 2: (2) Self-advocacy: People First movement, self-advocacy groups.
STEP 3: (3) Voting rights: most individuals with ID CAN vote (conservatorship may affect this — know your rights).
STEP 4: (4) Community inclusion: friendships, recreation, faith community, civic participation.
STEP 5: (5) Health advocacy: preventive care, mental health access, healthy aging (life expectancy for ID has increased dramatically but healthcare disparities persist).

CONTACT: THE ARC: thearc.org — policy advocacy, local chapters, community programs.
PEOPLE FIRST OF CA: peoplefirstofcalifornia.org — self-advocacy movement.
SCDD (State Council on Developmental Disabilities): scdd.ca.gov — policy advocacy, community inclusion.
ASAN (Autistic Self Advocacy Network): autisticadvocacy.org — neurodiversity and disability rights.
DRC: (800) 776-5746 — systemic advocacy, voting rights, community integration.
CA DDS: dds.ca.gov — Lanterman Act protection, DDS budget advocacy.
NATIONAL COUNCIL ON DISABILITY: ncd.gov — federal disability policy.

DOCUMENTS: ADVOCACY DOCUMENTS:
• Voter registration (individuals with ID have the RIGHT to vote in CA)
• Self-advocacy plan and goals
• People First membership
• The Arc membership and local chapter participation
• SCDD public comment and testimony records

POLICY TRACKING:
• Lanterman Act — CA's foundational disability rights law
• CA DDS budget (FY 2025-26: $18.7B, largest in history)
• HCBS Settings Rule compliance
• Employment First policy implementation
• Conservatorship reform legislation

HEALTHY AGING:
• Medical monitoring plan (ID-specific aging concerns)
• Down syndrome Alzheimer's screening (age 40+)
• Updated IPP reflecting changing needs

TIMELINE: Ongoing — lifelong.

AVOID: AVOID THESE COMMON PITFALLS: Isolation increases as person ages. Self-advocacy opportunities not offered. Voting rights restricted without basis. Health care providers lack training on ID. Aging with ID presents unique medical challenges. Policy changes affect services without family awareness.

RISKS: Isolation increases as person ages. Self-advocacy opportunities not offered. Voting rights restricted without basis. Health care providers lack training on ID. Aging with ID presents unique medical challenges. Policy changes affect services without family awareness.

RESOURCES: THE ARC: thearc.org — advocacy tools, policy updates, community inclusion, local chapters
FRCNCA: frcnca.org — peer support, advocacy training, language-accessible
UC DAVIS MIND INSTITUTE: health.ucdavis.edu/mindinstitute — peer groups, parent coaching, Spanish-language support
PARENTS HELPING PARENTS: php.com — consultations, webinars, support groups
DRC PUBLICATIONS: disabilityrightsca.org — RC rights, conservatorship, SSI guides (free, multilingual)
UCP: ucp.org — My Child Without Limits community
SELF-DETERMINATION PROGRAM: CA self-determination for RC clients
CA PTI NETWORK: parentcenterhub.org
BOOKS: 'The Complete Guide to Special Education' (Wilmshurst/Brue)

PRIMARY AGENCY: The Arc
Self-advocacy organizations
Regional Center
OTHER AGENCIES: DRC
