NATIONAL DISABILITY & EDUCATION RESOURCES

IDEA — Parents & Families
(U.S. Dept. of Education) [Law & SpEd Guidance]
  Official federal resource explaining parent rights under IDEA. Links families to federally funded Parent Training & Information Centers (PTIs) in every state. OSEP funds projects providing free inform
  Services: PTI/CPRC directory for every state, DC, PR, USVI, Pacific entities; IDEA topic-area resources; early learning resources; ECTA Center family resources; military-connected children resources; OCR civil 
  Cost: Free

Center for Parent Information & Resources (CPIR)
(parentcenterhub.org) [Law & SpEd Guidance]
  Central hub serving the national network of Parent Centers. Provides curated information, training materials, and resources to PTIs and CPRCs so they can serve families. Library of 1,100+ family-frien
  Services: Resource library searchable by topic (1,100+ items); 'New to Disability?' starting guides; IDEA training materials; OSEP glossaries (Spanish, Korean); parent participation guides for Early Interventio
  Cost: Free

Council of Parent Attorneys & Advocates (COPAA) [Law & SpEd Guidance]
  Independent nonprofit protecting civil rights of students with disabilities. Files amicus briefs and lawsuits in systemic cases of national significance. Provides online training for parents, advocate
  Services: Online training courses (SEAT certification program); weekly/monthly/quarterly roundtables by membership category; on-demand webinar library; attorney/advocate member directory; career center; Navigat
  Cost: Membership-based (tiered): Parent memberships available; some resources free to registered guests. 501(c)(3).

Parent to Parent USA (P2P USA) [Peer Support]
  National nonprofit supporting a network of Parent to Parent programs in all 50 states. Facilitates intentional one-to-one matches between trained volunteer Support Parents and parents seeking emotiona
  Services: One-to-one peer matching (parent-to-parent); trained Support Parent volunteer network; Alliance Member program quality standards; research-based matching practices; state affiliate network; Diversity,
  Cost: Free — all P2P programs are free to families

State Parent-to-Parent Organizations
(e.g., Georgia, Pennsylvania, Ohio, Massachusetts) [Peer Support]
  Local chapters of P2P USA offering localized peer connections, information specialists, support groups, and resource navigation. Each match evolves based on family needs — some are brief contacts, oth
  Services: One-to-one parent matching by diagnosis, age, and situation; trained support parent volunteers; referral to professional services when needed; Listening & Learning training for volunteers; affiliate p
  Cost: Free

Understood.org
(Learning & Thinking Differences) [Diagnosis-Specific]
  Major nonprofit (501(c)(3)) serving the 70 million people in the U.S. with learning and thinking differences. Provides free expert-driven guides, interactive simulations ('Through My Eyes'), community
  Services: Free articles/guides by topic (dyslexia, ADHD, IEP, 504, accommodations, AT); 'Through My Eyes' immersive simulations; ADHD Unstuck self-guided program; classroom accommodation lists (downloadable PDF
  Cost: Free — 501(c)(3) nonprofit

Hands & Voices
(Deaf/Hard of Hearing) [Diagnosis-Specific]
  Parent-driven nonprofit supporting families of children who are deaf or hard of hearing (D/HH) without bias toward any communication mode, method, or educational setting. Provides ASTra (Advocacy, Sup
  Services: ASTra educational advocacy program (trained advocates attend IEP meetings); Communication Considerations A-Z educational series; Communication Plan guidance for IEPs; school placement considerations g
  Cost: Free (chapter-based, some programs grant-funded)

Family Voices
(Special Health Care Needs) [Diagnosis-Specific]
  Family-led national organization promoting quality health care for children and youth with special health care needs (CYSHCN). Provides technical assistance to Family-to-Family Health Information Cent
  Services: Family-to-Family Health Information Center (F2F HIC) network in every state; healthcare system navigation assistance; insurance system guidance; peer-to-peer support; care coordination resources; Nati
  Cost: Free — F2F HICs are HRSA-funded, services free to families

National Center for Learning Disabilities (NCLD)
(ncld.org) [LD & Advocacy]
  Nonprofit focused on building community, sharing resources, and shaping policy for individuals with learning and attention issues. Partners with educators, students, families, and young adults to adva
  Services: Policy advocacy (federal/state); LD research reports and data; annual reports with impact data; family advocacy initiative (8-month training program with honorarium); LD Day of Action (Capitol Hill ad
  Cost: Free — 501(c)(3) nonprofit

Learning Disabilities Association of America (LDA)
(ldaamerica.org) [LD & Advocacy]
  Largest member-based nonprofit volunteer organization advocating for individuals with learning disabilities. Founded in 1964 by parents and professionals. 14,000-20,000 members organized into 200+ sta
  Services: State/local affiliate network (200+ chapters); annual international conference; LD Journal (peer-reviewed); Newsbriefs newsletter; LDA Podcast; sample letter to request school evaluation; informationa
  Cost: Membership-based (individual ~$25-40/year); many resources free to public. 501(c)(3).

Organization for Autism Research (OAR)
(researchautism.org) [Autism-Specific]
  Nonprofit dedicated to improving lives of autistic individuals by funding applied research that directly impacts day-to-day quality of life. Provides free, evidence-based resources and information to 
  Services: 'Life Journey Through Autism' guide series (free); 'A Parent's Guide to Research' (with Danya International); navigating research tips (evaluating evidence, identifying EBPs); classroom resource grant
  Cost: Free — all resources free to public. 501(c)(3).$kb$, $kb$resources$kb$, $kb$natl-res$kb$, $kb${"code":"natl-res","title":"National Disability Resources Directory","category":"resources","subcategory":"national","source_ref":"Entity Matrix v9.4","origin":"entity-matrix-v9.4"}$kb$::jsonb);

